      "content": "Interesting. So you're saying the grammar in B might actually make them seem less reliable in a courtroom compared to A? Doesn't the way someone speaks usually have nothing to do with whether they're actually telling the truth about what they saw? I'm wondering if the \"informal\" nature of B could be interpreted as being less precise or even less educated, which might sway a jury even if the facts are the same. What specific \"red flags\" would you point out to my students regarding B's language?",
